  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote a 3D breakout game in `src/main.ts` using `createAuraApp` on `#app`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so none of it has been run.\n\n- **Scene:** an 8x5 grid of bricks, a paddle and a ball, inside walls and a ceiling. Each row has its own color. Rows are worth 50, 40, 30, 20 and 10 points from the top. The scene uses the `neon-arcade` look.\n- **Controls:** Left/Right or A/D move the paddle, Space serves and R restarts at any time.\n- **Ball:** it bounces off the walls, ceiling, paddle and bricks. The paddle sets the outgoing angle by hit offset, up to 60° each way.\n- **Lives and status:** the player has 3 lives. After a miss the status goes back to `ready` and the ball waits on the paddle for Space. At 0 lives the status is `lost`. Clearing every brick sets `won`.\n- **HUD and overlay:** a DOM HUD below the canvas shows score, lives, status and a controls hint. A DOM overlay on top of the canvas shows YOU WIN or GAME OVER with a restart hint.\n- **State and readiness:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a getter returning `{status, score, lives, bricksLeft}`. `window.__TASK_READY__` is set to true one animation frame after my first game update.\n- **Loop:** my own `requestAnimationFrame` loop drives game logic in fixed 1/120 s steps and moves the nodes. The engine renders in its own loop. Removed bricks are hidden with `setVisible(false)`.\n\nI did not read the policy files outside the project that `AGENTS.md` points to. I stuck to `TASK.md`.\n\n",
